OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGNEW YUGOSLAV CEASEFIRE
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSET FOR WEDNESDAY
OL,5, The presidents of Serbia and Croatia
OL,6, and the Yugoslav federal defence
OL,7, minister have agreed on an absolute
OL,8, ceasefire as of 1300 BST tomorrow.
OL,10,FSlobodan Milosevic, Franjo Tudjman and
OL,11,FGeneral Veljko Kadijevic reached the
OL,12,Fagreement at EC-brokered peace talks
OL,13,Fin Igalo, Montenegro.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FLord Carrington, who chaired the EC
OL,16,Fpeace talks, said the new ceasefire was
OL,17,Fsettled after several hours of talks
OL,18,Fwith the three warring factions.
OL,20,FHe said everyone agreed Yugoslavia had
OL,21,Fbeen days away from irretrievable war,
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789673634
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGBATTLES RAGE ON
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGIN CROATIA
OL,5, Fierce clashes are continuing in the
OL,6, republic of Croatia despite the latest
OL,7, Yugoslav ceasefire agreement.
OL,9,FThe Croatian authorities accused
OL,10,Fairforce planes of attacking a suburb
OL,11,Fof Zagreb and Croatian radio reported
OL,12,Fland and air bombardments on Osijek.
OL,14,FBelgrade radio reported clashes in
OL,15,FVukovar, with federal forces breaking
OL,16,Fthe Croatian blockade on barracks there
OL,18,FFighting is also continuing in the
OL,19,Fsouth-west of the republic, as Yugoslav
OL,20,Fnavy ships continue a blockade of
OL,21,FCroatia's seven main ports.
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789673634
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGYUGOSLAV NAVY BLOCKADES
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCROATIAN PORTS
OL,5, As news of the latest ceasefire accord
OL,6, came, Yugoslav navy ships kept up a
OL,7, blockade of Croatia's main ports.
OL,9,FThis followed an army operation
OL,10,Flaunched yesterday to free military
OL,11,Fbases taken over by Croats.
OL,13,FSeven Adriatic ports were affected,
OL,14,Ffrom Rijeka in the north to Dubrovnik
OL,15,Fand Split in the south. Reports from
OL,16,FSplit spoke of some five vessels
OL,17,Fpatrolling outside.
OL,19,FThere were also reports of fighting
OL,20,Fjust north of Split, around the port of
OL,21,FSibenik.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
