OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789673634
OL,1,Vk4                               G7/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGJUDITH WARD BOMBING
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCASE REOPENED
OL,4,D
OL,5, Home Secretary Kenneth Baker has sent
OL,6, the case of convicted IRA bomber Judith
OL,7, Ward to the Court of Appeal.
OL,9,FShe was convicted over the bombing of a
OL,10,Fcoach on the M62 in 1974 and given life
OL,11,Fsentences for the murder of each of
OL,12,Fthe 12 people who died in the attack.
OL,14,FWard has never appealed but Mr Baker
OL,15,Facted after a Home Office review of the
OL,16,Fscientific evidence.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe case against her was also based on
OL,19,Fconfession evidence that she was linked
OL,20,Fwith the IRA, though the IRA denied she
OL,21,Fwas a member.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789673634
OL,1,Vk4                               G8/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGBIRMINGHAM SIX'S RELEASE
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGLED TO WARD DECISION
OL,4,D
OL,5, The Home Secretary says the referral of
OL,6, Judith Ward's case to the Appeal Court
OL,7, followed a Home Office review after the
OL,8, release of the Birmingham Six.
OL,10,FKenneth Baker said he had made the
OL,11,Fdecision in the light of the scientific
OL,12,Fevidence in the Six case, particularly
OL,13,Fthat of scientist Dr Frank Skuse.
OL,15,FDr Skuse, whose forensic evidence was
OL,16,Fdiscredited in the Six's appeal, also
OL,17,Fconducted tests in the Ward case.
OL,19,FIt is the fourth time in 18 months a
OL,20,Fcase stemming from the IRA bombings in
OL,21,Fthe 1970s has been reopened.
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
