OL,1,Vk4                               G9/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGKINNOCK FORECASTS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGNOVEMBER ELECTION
OL,5, Labour leader Neil Kinnock has told the
OL,6, shadow cabinet he believes there will
OL,7, be an autumn general election.
OL,9,FAt a meeting in London to decide on
OL,10,FLabour's election strategy, Mr Kinnock
OL,11,Fsaid he expected John Major to "cut
OL,12,Fand run" in November.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FLabour would be ready for a November
OL,15,Felection, he promised, and winning it
OL,16,Fwould be a "straightforward" matter.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FDeputy leader Roy Hattersley said
OL,19,FLabour's private opinion polls showed
OL,20,Fit 1% ahead of the Tories - but given a
OL,21,Fmargin of error they were neck-and-neck
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789673634
OL,1,Vk4                              G10/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGCONSERVATIVES AND LABOUR
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGLEVEL IN NEW POLL
OL,4,D
OL,5, The Conservatives and Labour are
OL,6, running neck-and-neck, according to a
OL,7, new opinion poll.
OL,9,FBut the ICM poll in tomorrow's Guardian
OL,10,Fprovides more evidence that Labour has
OL,11,Flost ground - plunging six points over
OL,12,Fthe past month, with the Tories wiping
OL,13,Fout a nine-point deficit.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FThe Conservatives (up 3%) and Labour
OL,16,Fare on 39%, the Liberal Democrats on
OL,17,F17% (up 1%), and others on 5%.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThe survey polled 1,387 voters in 103
OL,20,Fconstituencies on Saturday, Sunday and
OL,21,FMonday.
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
