OL,1,Vk4                              G11/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGBAKER OFFER TO ISRAEL
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGOVER US LOANS ROW
OL,5, US Secretary of State James Baker has
OL,6, put forward a series of proposals to
OL,7, Israel aimed at ending the dispute over
OL,8, $10 billion of US loan guarantees.F
OL,10,FThe US wants any request for guarantees
OL,11,F- for loans to resettle Soviet Jews -
OL,12,Fpostponed for four months so as not to
OL,13,Fharm the Middle East peace process.
OL,15,FAfter leaving for Egypt, Mr Baker said
OL,16,Fthat if Israel accepted this, the US
OL,17,Fwould not seek any further delay.
OL,19,FHe said the US would try to compensate
OL,20,FIsrael for any losses suffered during
OL,21,Fthe delay.
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11812
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789673634
OL,1,Vk4                              G12/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGUS LETTER DISCUSSED
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGBY PALESTINIANS
OL,4,D
OL,5, US Secretary of State James Baker has
OL,6, given both Israelis and Palestinians
OL,7, letters of assurance on basic rules for
OL,8, a Middle East peace conference.
OL,10,FIn Jerusalem, Mr Baker met Palestinian
OL,11,Frepresentatives from the occupied
OL,12,Fterritories to discuss the document.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FPalestinian delegate Faisal Husseini
OL,15,Fsaid it had given certain guarantees.
OL,16,FThe Palestine Liberation Organisation
OL,17,Fis meeting to consider its response.
OL,19,FMeanwhile, Soviet deputy foreign
OL,20,Fminister Alexander Belonogov is to meet
OL,21,FPLO leader Yasser Arafat over the issue
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG17-09-91F  teletextarchive.com
